---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/SectionLabel.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Darío Kozicki" description="About Darío Kozicki, a senior software engineer based in Buenos Aires.">
  <div class="page-shell interior-page">
    <header class="page-intro about-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I’m curious about how things work and skeptical of answers that stop too early.</h1>
      <p>I’m a software engineer based in Buenos Aires. Over seven years I’ve worked across healthcare, recruiting, consulting, e-commerce, and banking, moving between product code, backend systems, data, and infrastructure as the problem required.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="about-section">
      <SectionLabel label="How I work" />
      <div class="about-columns">
        <p>I tend to zoom out. A database decision is also a reliability decision, a cost decision, an ownership decision, and eventually a debugging problem for someone who was not in the room.</p>
        <p>I enjoy understanding the theoretically correct version of a system, then deciding how much of it the situation actually needs. Sometimes the right architecture is less architecture.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <SectionLabel label="Systems I’ve worked on" />
      <div class="systems-list">
        <div><strong>Financial &amp; operations</strong><p>Banking applications, ETL processes, SQL, and REST/SOAP integrations.</p></div>
        <div><strong>High-volume commercial systems</strong><p>Marketplace campaign and seller workflows, queues, SQL/NoSQL storage, and event-specific discounts.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Regulated data</strong><p>Healthcare modernization, regional PII/PHI handling, and safer service boundaries.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Platform engineering</strong><p>AWS, RDS, Terraform, SST, Docker, serverless services, and FinOps analysis.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <SectionLabel label="Opinions, held normally" />
      <div class="about-columns">
        <p>I’m comfortable questioning an established direction, including one proposed by someone more senior. I’m equally interested in finding out that I’m wrong.</p>
        <p>I care about the capability behind a title or credential more than the label itself. The same standard applies to my own claims.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <SectionLabel label="Credentials & communication" />
      <div class="credential-list">
        <p><strong>AWS Certified Solutions Architect — Associate</strong><span>2026</span></p>
        <p><strong>Systems Engineering · National Technological University</strong><span>2025</span></p>
        <p><strong>Speaker · React Global Summit</strong><span>2023</span></p>
        <p><strong>Spanish · Native / English · C2</strong><span>Languages</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <p class="archive-note">Curious about earlier experiments? <a class="text-link" href="/archive/">Visit the project archive →</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
